ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Solving the systems of equations simultaneously, we get
\[
\begin{cases}
y=x+3\\
y=\frac{-2}{x}
\end{cases}
\]
which yields
\[
\begin{cases}
x=-1\\
y=2
\end{cases}
\]
or
\[
\begin{cases}
x=-2\\
y=1
\end{cases}
\]
Since the coordinates of point C are $(-1, 2)$,\\
therefore, the coordinates of point D are $\boxed{(-2, 1)}$.

